# WolkaraForever layer patch 0065 - audio: the game's sound without iOS's HAL (a model of one output device)
#
# Why: a power measurement on an iPad Pro 11-inch (M5), iPadOS 26.5 (18 Nov 2026), found a thread in the dispatch queue
# com.apple.BTAudioHALPlugin at 25 % of a core at every step, unchanged with all of the game's sound off
# (Sound_EnableAllSound 0 took 10 %, all of it the main thread's), while iOS's HAL plug-ins were loaded in the game's
# process (BasebandVoice, BuiltinAudioPlugin, AppleTimeSyncAudioClock, BTAudioHALPlugin, NetworkUplinkClock,
# OctaviaHalogen, AirPlayHalogen) and no Bluetooth audio device was connected. The game's sound engine asks the macOS
# HAL for its output (AudioHardwareAddPropertyListener dOut/dIn/dev#, AudioHardwareGetProperty dOut/dIn,
# AudioDeviceGetProperty name/srnd/nsrt/fsz#), and both adapters handed those calls to iOS's CoreAudio, whose HAL then
# ran in the process with all of its plug-ins. The sound never needed it: it plays through RemoteIO on the session.
#
# With WolkaraForeverAudioAvoidHAL on (the default; AKAudioModel.h, overlaid into translation/AKSupport) the CoreAudio
# adapter answers from a model of one output device - the session's route, under AKAudioModelDevice - the way iOS's
# HAL answered on the iPad: one device for the default output and input, an empty legacy device list, the route's
# name, rate and IO buffer, a stereo channel layout; listeners are taken and never called (the device never changes;
# RemoteIO follows a new route itself); the property API keeps its answers under the model's ID. The AudioToolbox
# adapter gives RemoteIO the model's device. A call the model cannot answer still goes to iOS, with iOS's ID for the
# default output, and is logged ("audio: HAL fallback (...)"), so the game keeps its sound. Off is exactly the old
# path. Logs: "audio: HAL avoided (RemoteIO)" / "audio: RemoteIO with its device from iOS's HAL (... is off)" and
# "audio: HAL model answers the game ..." / "audio: HAL in use (WolkaraForeverAudioAvoidHAL is off)".
# TKCoreAudioHALForwards / TKAudioToolboxHALForwards count the calls handed to iOS's HAL (tests).
#
# Applies after: 0005-coreaudio-keep-session.patch, 0037-gate-recurring-diagnostics.patch
# Applies to: translation/CoreAudio/Hardware.m, translation/AudioToolbox/Output.m
# Upstream: candidate (the iPad showed the plug-ins gone and the sound fine, 18 Nov 2026).
#
